// INTRO 
"Val.Introduction": "Hey, Farmer. Be careful, there's an abundance of Rock Crabs in East Scarp - tainted and otherwise. A crabundance, if you will.$23#$b#I shouldn't quit my day job as a dungeon delver, my jokes are in ruins.$23",
// COMMUNITY CENTER BUNDLES  
"Val.JojaBegin": "It doesn't surprise me that Joja was able to buy out the Community Center. That's capitalism at work, I suppose.$24",
"Val.CCBegin": "Have you started revitalizing the Community Center, @? That's a noble effort. Good luck!$1",
"Val.CCBus": "Nice job, @! The bus will make it much easier to go to the desert. I haven't been to the Skull Cavern in a while, I should sharpen my swords.$31",
"Val.CCMinecart": "So you're saying you can hop in a mine cart and navigate all over The Valley with it? That sounds safe.$29",
"Val.CCComplete": "Congratulations on all your hard work, @. It's so nice to see the Community Center up and running again, it's been ages since anyone acknowledged it.$26",
"Val.MovieTheater": "Wanna go see a flick, @? It's my treat, since you're the one who went through all the trouble to rebuild from those ruins.$1#$b#Nothing does your arteries as good as an evening full of Flavacol popcorn!$20",
// BIRTHDAYS
"Val.BirthdayReminder.Hector": "I was stumped on what to get for Hector's birthday until I noticed [LocalizedText Strings/DN.SnS:HimHer] just laying face-first in the dirt the other day. Bar of soap it is.$27",
"Val.BirthdayReminder.Coriander": "So, question. Do we sing Coriander the 'happy birthday' song? I don't know about you, but I'd get stage fright singing in front of an award winning vocalist.$22",
"Val.BirthdayReminder.Roslin": "Roslin's birthday is coming up. I'm proud to say I'm wise enough to know not to ask her age. I love not getting fireballs thrown at my face. $1",
"Val.BirthdayReminder.Dandelion": "Dandelion's birthday is just around the corner, and my brilliant plan is to challenge her to a contest of strength. I know I'll lose, because that woman's a brick house, but it's the thought that counts.$0",
"Val.BirthdayReminder.Arden": "I thought getting Arden a gift would be difficult, being a dragon and all. Turns out, her interest in alcohol is extremely stereotypical, so I just let her raid my liquor cabinet.$25",
// END OF SEASON
"Val.SpringEnd": "Wow, Spring's over and done with already... Did you have a productive open to the year? Guess you'll be busy preparing the fields for Summer, huh?$20",
"Val.SummerEnd": "Suppose your summer crops are about ready to die off, @? That's alright. Just means it's time for a change; hardly a bad thing.$17",
"Val.FallEnd": "Winter's coming... Can't say I'm looking forward to it, but Spring will come back to us eventually.$27",
"Val.WinterEnd": "Thank goodness. The sun will shine on us again soon enough. Looking forward to the change of season.$25",
// SVE COMMUNITY DAY
"Val.CommunityCenter.1": "I'm so glad the everyone makes the effort to spend time together here. Stuff like this makes The Valley feel like home.$26",
"Val.CommunityCenter.2": "Good to see you here, @. Just doing the rounds and catching up with everyone. Sometimes it's hard to make time to see your friends, so I'm glad the townsfolk are committed to gathering together like this once a season.$20",
"Val.CommunityCenter.3": "Honestly, it's nice to be able to catch up with Marlon. Me and the old man don't get to hang out much outside of work. This is like, the only time I don't get a lecture on safe dungeon delving.$23",
// FESTIVALS (DAY BEFORE)
"Val.EggFestival": "The egg festival is tomorrow! The first big event to ring in the new year, huh? Hope your egg-hunting skills are sharp, @, I hear you've got some pretty tough competition.$17",
"Val.FlowerDance": "I love dancing, actually. I was big into the club scene back in college, but... Well, that's a very different sort of dancing, usually with a lot more liquor.$27",
"Val.Luau": "Tradition is important, of course, but doesn't it just seem really short sighted to blindly throw a ton of different things into one soup? I love taking risks, but that seems a little much.$27",
"Val.MoonlightJelly": "Tomorrow's celebration is my second favorite, next to Spirit's Eve. I can see the Jellies from the cove from right outside my house. It's breathtaking.$4",
"Val.SDVFair": "The fair is tomorrow, @! Are you going to bring pumpkins?$31#$b#I'm just saying, if I was voting and it was all pumpkins, you'd win.$23",
"Val.SpiritsEve": "So, there are a few rules to be followed on Spirit's Eve, back from when I was a kid.$17#$b#One, always check your candy. Two, always wear a costume. Three, always have treats on hand to give out.$23#$b#Finally, never blow out a Jack o' Lantern before midnight. That's the most important one.$31",
"Val.IceFestival": "Festival of Ice tomorrow, huh? I'm not one for fishing, by any means. But I can throw a mean snowball - and, hey, if you can dodge an Iridium Bat...$22",
"Val.NightMarket": "Oh, that's right. The Night Market's going on! I'd forgotten.$1#$b#Maybe I'll stop by and see if they've got anything from Gotoro for sale. Someone's bound to have smuggled in something interesting.$20",
"Val.WinterStar": "I don't like Winter, but I love giving gifts. If I can't pull off a grand gesture, I try to be as specific to the recipient as I can.$4",
// ROMANTIC (NEGATIVE)
"Val.Breakup": "Oh, s- @, I'm sorry you feel that way. And I'm sorry if I've done something to lead you to this decision.$24#$b#Hopefully, with enough time, we can be friends again. But I understand if you'd like space for a while.$25",
"Val.Divorced ": "%Angry, still half in love with you, and tremendously sorry - they turn away.",  
"Val.SpouseFarmhouseClutter": "Hey, it's pretty cluttered in here. Would you mind tidying up some of your stuff?$24",
"Val.SpouseMonstersInHouse": "Stand back, @! There's creatures afoot!$3",
"Val.WipedMemory": "Hey, uh!... Huh, sorry. For a second, I thought I knew you. Hm. I had a joke to make, but...$7#$b#It's in... ruins? That doesn't make any sense. Uh, anyway...$6", 
// ROMANTIC (POSITIVE)
"Val.SpouseGiftJealous": "It was so thoughtful of you to give {0} a {1}! This is why I love you, @.$4", 
"Val.Stardrop": "I found this growing in the Quarry Mine, believe it or not. I hope it tastes as good as you do.$4",
// RESORT
"Val.Resort.1": "Just taking a little break from running around, @. Be sure to put on some sunscreen if you're going to spend a lot of time out and about.$17",
"Val.Resort.2": "I could probably fall asleep here, but I sleep like a rock and I'd probably miss the boat back...$27",
"Val.Resort.3": "One nice thing about the beach is getting to show off all the scars. I got a lot of them from adventuring, but I'll admit I'm most proud of the ones on my chest.$10",
// GREEN RAIN
"Val.GreenRain": "I've never seen rain like this before, even with all the time I spent in Pelican Town as a kid. I hope it's a good omen.$22",
"Val.GreenRainFinished": "The rain was pretty intense, but it didn't seem to have any negative side effects. Everything is so lush right now, I'm sure Hector's excited.$26",
"Val.GreenRain2": "Now that I've gotten to know Hector a bit more, I'm pretty convinced this is [LocalizedText Strings/DN.SnS:HisHers] doing.$27",
// POLYAMORY 
"Val.MarriedMonogamousNPC": "Sorry, @! I'm flattered, but you're with a monogamous partner, so I'd be intruding on the rules of your relationship...$29",
// TRASH REACT 
"Val.DumpsterDiveComment": "If you wanted to dig for treasure, you could try... uh, the Mines, and not the trash?$27",
// SLINGSHOT 
"Val.HitBySlingshot": "Ow! Watch your aim, stay in the range if you're an amateur!$21",
// LOCATION ENTRIES 
"Val.VillageInn": "Rosa, you make a damn fine cup of coffee./It's so homey in here./Why are the floors covered in hay?", 
"Val.ArtificerHouse": "Home sweet home...!/Time to get back to working on my campaign./My dogs are barking...",
"Val.EastScarp": "Oh, there's the smell of sea air./Was that a Rock Crab?/This town has so many good sitting spots...",
"Val.Underforge": "Nothing beats a sword fresh off the anvil./Man, it's real hot down here.../Time to get some work done!",
// LOW HEART
"Val.Generic.1": "You pick up skills really quickly, @. It's super impressive, and I commend you for your dedication to learning so many different things.$0",
"Val.Generic.2": "Wilderness Golems are especially ornery when they're on the surface, most of all when the weather is nice.$29#$b#At least they're easier to manage than Stone Golems. Keep an eye out for them, they hit pretty hard.$27",
"Val.Generic.3": "Are you a sword, hammer, or dagger sort of person? Be sure to maintenance your weapon, especially if the weather is poor or if you're heavy handed with it.$26",
"Val.Generic.4": "Crabs keep breaking into my house. Stygium crabs, sure. But also Rock Crabs. And regular crabs.$15",
"Val.Generic.5": "Keep your chin up, @. Even if today is a bit on the rough side, tomorrow always has a chance of being better.",
"Val.Generic.6": "Seen anything fun on your adventures, @? Big ol' monsters? Weird plants? Sordid affairs between townsfolk? I'd love to listen over a drink of your choice.$10",
"Val.Generic.7": "The desert trader has these artifact troves; they've got things like Dwarven Gadgets and other relics inside. Problem is, I'm not sure how it's all sourced.$11",
"Val.Generic.8": "I picked a scab from an injury I got fighting monsters, which... just made it worse. I do this every time, without fail. Don't pick your wounds, @.$29",
"Val.Generic.9": "I love watching the sun rise. Waking up early is something of a bummer, but the shimmering gleam of sunlight on the surface of the ocean is worth it.$4",
"Val.Generic.10": "Did you know Frost Bats have trouble surviving in humid temperatures? You're not likely to see them on the surface. Fruit Bats, though? We've got several colonies of those.$26",
"Val.Generic.11": "What's under a Metal Head helmet, anyway? I've always wondered, but I've never gone out of my way to go try and pry one apart. Some mysteries are better left unsolved.$27",
"Val.Generic.12": "When I first started delving as a kid, I was particularly fascinated by the Dust Sprites. Cute little things, aren't they?$9#$b#Wish they weren't such a good way to gather coal, though.$2",
"Val.Generic.13": "I'm currently trying to source a game called Batlavania: Rondo of Blood. It hasn't been released here in Ferngill, but I've played the sequel and now I'm hooked on the gameplay.",
"Val.Generic.14": "Hiking in the Deep Mountains is fantastic. There's so much to see, there's weird goats to pet - I'm not sure I could ask for more, honestly. And! There's the north shore, which has a brilliant view.$26",
"Val.Generic.15": "There must be something up with the lightbulb on the pier on the main Scarp beach. I swear, it's green sometimes...$29",
"Val.Generic.16": "I've seen and heard of a lot of strange supernatural phenomenons up on the surface, cryptids and the like. Really, I think it's just monsters with varying abilities and levels of intelligence.$22",
"Val.Generic.17": "Have you ever seen a Squid Kid? I'm not sure why they're even called that. They don't look like squids but they DO shoot fireballs. Take care if you run into one, @. $29",
"Val.Generic.18": "I think the Golden Masks you can occasionally find in the Skull Cave are ceremonial versions of the ones worn by Shadow Shamans.$22#$b#I haven't met a Shadow Folk from Calico Desert, but I don't doubt they exist.$23",
"Val.Generic.19": "Every day, give yourself a present. It could be a nice new shirt, or a little nap, or half a pot of fresh coffee all to yourself! Don't ignore your own happiness for the sake of others, @.$25",
"Val.Generic.20": "There was this one time I watched a Stygium Rex try to eat an ore node. I just... that's only going to make the corruption worse! Stop licking the damn thing!$27",
"Val.Generic.21": "I love parties. I love dancing, strong drinks, loud music. I'll go to ZuZu city to surround myself with strangers. After all, The larger the crowd, the more intimate it is.$17",
"Val.Generic.22": "I have a certain fondness for trinkets. Things from movies and books, mostly. I don't mind wearing my interests on my sleeve; it's vulnerable, and helps start conversations.$1",
"Val.Generic.23": "Do you like horror movies, @? We should watch one sometime. I love the classic slashers, but my favorite is about a Trick or Treater who enforces the rules of Spirit's Eve...$23",
"Val.Generic.24": "I haven't experimented enough to be entirely sure, but I suspect that Stygium is comparable to arsenic and cadmium in terms of it's toxicity. It's not something you want exposure to for long.$27",
"Val.Generic.25": "The plant in my museum wasn't tainted to start. I had it since I first starting collecting weird Stygium stuff, but didn't think to encase them right away...$27",
"Val.Generic.26": "The water in the Deep Dark is unfortunately as corrupted as the creatures that dwell in the caverns. It's an ecological disaster down there, in every sense.$2",
"Val.Generic.27": "I have an insatiable lust for crab cakes. I know what I must do... and East Scarp will provide.$32",
"Val.Generic.28": "When I read stories, I tend to appreciate narratives that read more like character studies. It's fun to really delve into someone's psyche to understand their perspective.$0#$b#You can take it a step further and understand the context behind why a story was written. Sometimes things like time period matter, and I just think that's neat.$1",
"Val.Generic.29": "I was re-reading one of my favorite Warrens & Wyverns setting supplements recently, Curse of Vlahd. It's a horror-tragedy about a party of adventurers being tormented by a vampire...$26",
"Val.Generic.30": "One of the games that I have, that I never run, is Vampire the Facade. If I'm going to do something with creatures of the night, it would be Curse of Vlahd.$29",
"Val.Generic.31": "Sometimes, I like to make casts of dice sets and make custom ones out of resin. It's really fun, and you can do a lot of interesting colors. I'll try metal ones next!$1",
"Val.Generic.32": "Hope you're able to get some recreational reading in, @. It's good for the brain, good for the heart. You can borrow off my shelves, if you'd like.$25",
"Val.Generic.33": "I've been marathoning my favorite movies lately. The Pharaoh, Colorado Jones, Treasure Universe... What are yours, @?$26",
"Val.Generic.34": "My horns? They're made of keratin, like nails are. Painting them actually protects them. Sometimes I go with orange, sometimes I go with clear coat.$17",
"Val.Generic.35": "I have a tail, but I keep it tucked into my pants. If I'm not tripping on it, someone's stepping on it. If someone's not stepping on it, a monster's trying to bite it...$27",
"Val.Generic.36": "I tore my pillow in my sleep on accident. Horn got caught on it...$11#$b#Aw, well. Good excuse as any to get a newer, fluffier one.$10",
"Val.Generic.37": "I've traveled a lot, but the seasons here are a lot more drastic than what I've seen elsewhere. I like that, though. It's part of The Valley's character.$1",
"Val.Generic.38": "A skeleton nicked me real good in the shoulder the other day. Do they use the bones of their fallen brethren to throw at their opponents? Hilarious, but morbid.$27",
"Val.Generic.39": "Do you go to the hot springs in the mountains often? I've been up that way a few times, mostly at night. It's good for the muscles. You exert yourself a lot, be sure to give yourself grace.$25",
"Val.Generic.40": "I'm trying to cut down on my caffeine consumption. So when I get up, I only have one cup of coffee. And then I have another with breakfast...$0#$e#And usually I've got one in a to-go cup on the way to the Deep Dark. And then that's it for the day...$6#$e#Oh, besides the one I have with lunch, you've got to have one with lunch. And then an espresso around two, you know, to chase off the inevitable migraine... and THEN that's it...$15#$e#Except for the one I have when I get home, and the one right before bed... So, yeah! Really been cutting back. Very proud of myself.$17",
"Val.Generic.41": "Making chainmail is a time consuming process. I forged rings and wove them together with pliers. Now, all I have to do is repair the shirt once in a while.$20",
"Val.Generic.42": "Technically, farriers specialize in metalworking associated with hooves, not blacksmiths. I learned to do both because I love horseshoes - they're a symbol of good luck!$25",
"Val.Generic.43": "When swinging a blacksmith hammer, you do want to lift it above your head and then swing. More force is better to move the steel in a short time before the blade cools.$1",
"Val.Generic.44": "I'm pretty sure smithing and adventuring keep me in shape, but smithing is less about being able to lift a heavy hammer and more about being able to slam a light one down a thousand times.$28",
"Val.Generic.45": "I love working with leather, but my favorite part of the process is tooling. I can space out and lose myself in detailing. Mostly, I enjoy floral designs!$1",
"Val.Generic.46": "Things I've made from leather? My armor, smithing apron, belts, gloves, holsters. And... plenty of other stuff. Leather is terribly versatile. $28",
"Val.Generic.47": "If you asked me to pick between Cherry Pie and Pumpkin Pie, I wouldn't be able to. Great pie and warm coffee really invoke a sense of nostalgia for me.$4",
"Val.Generic.48": "I stopped in at Rosa's and she had freshly made Maple Bars. Like any logical person, I bought three and ate two right there with a cup of coffee. The last one's for after dinner.$1",
"Val.Generic.49": "How do I take my coffee? Black as midnight on a moonless night. But sometimes, I add a drop of Salish Bourbon as a little present for the day.$17",
"Val.Generic.50": "I've considered moving back to the Fern Islands, where I went to school. But outside The Valley, there's a vast carelessness that I don't think I can adapt to.$2",
"Val.Generic.51": "Hey @! I found this down below, and thought you might be interested.$1 [96 97 98 99 100 101 103 104 105 106 108 109 110 111 112 113 115 116 117 118 119 120 121 122 123]",
"Val.Generic.52": "Hey, @! I met with the desert trader - I had some unusual minerals they were looking for, so we did a little exchange. This is an excellent study piece! [124 125]$1",
"Val.Generic.53": "Hey, @. I dug up a fossil, check it out!$1[586 587 588 589]",
"Val.Generic.54": "Hey, @! I've got a bone to pick with- nah, just kidding. Just found something down below you might need for the museum.$17 [579 580 581 582 583 584 585]",
"Val.Generic.55": "Hey, @! I found something weird on Ginger Island. I think it might be of use to you.$26[820 821 822 823 824 825 826 827 828]",
// HIGH HEART
"Val.Generic.56": "My childhood tabletop character's name was Gideon Weaveforger. Clearly he stuck with me, since I ended up going to school for metallurgical engineering. It was probably really healthy to have an outlet for a fledgling interest.#$b#I miss him, in a way. Because now I run games eternally instead of playing them... Maybe I can sneak him in as a cameo.",
"Val.Generic.57": "I'm an Artificer, but I hold the title 'Doctor'. I mean, I AM a Doctor, just not THAT kind of Doctor. I have a doctorate.#$b#It's not the same thing. You can't help people with a doctorate. You just sit there and you're useless!",
"Val.Generic.58": "Back when I was in college, I was the president of the board gaming club. We managed to repeatedly secure funding to buy games and supplements and then test them out. Not sure that's how the finances should've worked...#$b#But, we had a great time, and we even funded a few trips to local conventions and tried to volunteer for them when we could.",
"Val.Generic.59": "You should come over for cocktails sometime, @. Or mocktails, if that's your preference. I enjoy making drinks, it's a way for me to express my hospitality.#$b#Most of the time, I want my drinks neat. But I'm also big on things that are citrus forward; I've a soft spot for kettle sours... ",
"Val.Generic.60": "Did you know that skeletons can do magic? I didn't either, until one of them froze my feet to the floor. He even had a cape on. It billowed dramatically behind him as he charged at me.#$b#Goes to show it's always worth approaching the mines with caution. Stay safe, @. ",
"Val.Generic.61": "We don't know much about how Mummies animate, since the only way to incapacitate them is with bombs and that doesn't leave much to study.#$b#Capturing a live Mummy seems needlessly cruel, so unfortunately the best we can do is study the strange tombs they tend to wander after they've been dealt with. I'd love to take it a step further than that, but I don't want to get cursed.",
"Val.Generic.62": "Have you ever seen those Dwarvish Sentries inside the volcano on Ginger Island? For all that they're slow, they come at you with reckless abandon. Clearly, the Dwarves had something they want to protect somewhere in there.#$b#It's worth exploring, but be careful navigating that place, @, I wouldn't want to hear secondhand about anything happening to you.",
"Val.Generic.63": "I suspect there are variants of Pepper Rexes we haven't seen yet. For example, a lot of the bones we find in prehistoric spaces don't match the living specimens, but they're dated within the last twenty years.#$b#There are Stygium Rexes in the Deep Dark, but I expect there's more, since those are normal Pepper Rexes, just corrupted...",
"Val.Generic.64": "Do you know what the bottom half of a Duggy looks like? It's been on my mind all day. For all we know, they can be serpentine, and nobody's bothered to pull one up out of the hole and check.#$b#While I respect that the academic community hasn't deemed this important, I respectfully disagree with their decision. That being said, we should go uproot some Duggies.",
"Val.Generic.65": "I'm not sold on it yet, but there's a substantial amount of anthropological evidence supporting the hypothesis that Goblins and Dwarves are related. It's just a theory, though!#$b#I think it's interesting but a lot of it's circumstantial. Personally, lean into the idea that they cohabited before the Elemental Wars rather than stem from the same exact ancestor.",
"Val.Generic.66": "I really want to know how a Treasure Chest can wind up in a Ghost Fish pond. Ponds are man-made, so where are they getting them from? They can't go treasure hunting, fish don't even have thumbs. Or am I just overthinking?$27",
"Val.Generic.67": "I've always wanted a big library in my house, kind of like in the movies. I mean, it's a mix of textbooks, fiction and tabletop supplements, but books are books. It doesn't matter what you read as long as you enjoy it.#$b#You're more than welcome to borrow something, @. And, unlike Gunther, I don't hold grudges over late fees...",
"Val.Generic.68": "There are difficult to decipher messages on the walls of the Skull Cavern. Have you ever noticed them, @? Something about heroes. Maybe we can go together and have a look; I'm sure there's something interesting to be discovered there.#$b#There are also really strange skeletons in the desert that I'd love to take a closer look at. Draconic remains are far and few in between...",
"Val.Generic.69": "So I climbed through the hatch on the roof of The Guild and watched the sunset last night. Beer in hand, just listening to the waves. It was amazing. There's something really special about The Valley, @.#$b#You should join me sometime. It's a really special view, and I'm more than happy to share it.",
"Val.Generic.70": "I got bitten up by one of those flying Serpents in the Skull Cave. Those things are fierce, aren't they? I'd rather deal with an entire horde of skeletons. They're slower, and they don't swarm.#$b#Some skeletons can do magic, which is frustrating, but Serpents are so vicious in their pursuit I don't think they're comparable.",
"Val.Generic.71": "15 some-odd years adventuring will leave you with a lot of scars. I was self-conscious of them at first, but now they're a point of pride - Even the new ones.#$b#I feel like that particular injury was actually a turning point; I feel like I was set on a different path after you patched me up.",
"Val.Generic.72": "Sometimes I find old arms deep in the mines. Swords, hammers and the like. I can't help but wonder if the ghosts that haunt those spaces are just trying to warn newer adventurers, like they don't want them to share the same fate.#$b#I've never been one for looting - things that are of value belong in a museum, and ore veins are for everyone. So I tend to just leave old equipment where it is.",
"Val.Generic.73": "My depth perception isn't great on the right side. It does make delving a little harder, as if I didn't have to be careful before...#$b#Sometimes I feel very sensitive to the light, but that's nothing an eyepatch can't address.",
"Val.Generic.74": "I've had fire-eyes as long as I can remember; I assume it's something to do with being a Troll. I've been a bit disappointed at how I've lost color in one, but most everyone has reassured me that it scarred over well.",
"Val.Generic.75": "The worst part of that big injury I got wasn't my eye. Really, the major side effect is the occasional headache right in the socket.#$b#It's nothing unmanageable, but it's been a frustrating adjustment to make. ",
"Val.Generic.76": "I spend a lot of time learning about my friend's interests so that I can incorporate their favorite themes and tropes into my Warrens & Wyverns game.#$b#It brings me a lot of joy to be able to write scenarios and narratives that are satisfying, and grow their characters emotionally.",
"Val.Generic.77": "Stayed up all night playing Batlavania. Do I regret it? No. The soundtrack is bomb, and the art is fantastic.#$b#Grim fantasy is one of my favorite genres, although I don't tend to go very dark in my Warrens & Wyverns game unless I talk it out with the players first.",
"Val.Generic.78": "Warrens & Wyverns is published by a company called Sorcerers of the Sound; they've been making games since I was a little kid. I've played every edition - some are better than others.#$b#I also really like Charged by the Cataclysm games, oh! And you can't forget the all time tabletop classic, Westlands!",
"Val.Generic.79": "My tail getting in the way of everything is really annoying. I just do my best to keep it wrapped around my leg. The horns don't really bother me though, even if it's difficult to sleep sometimes.#$b#Nobody in The Valley has ever given me an issue about the extra appendages, but unfortunately the folks in the Fern Islands weren't so receptive. I suppose they don't have a mountain range, so Trolls wouldn't be drawn there normally.",
"Val.Generic.80": "I got my horseshoe tattoo after I graduated. I'm glad none of my adventuring incidents have damaged it; I got it over some old scar tissue, so I'd rather not have another layer of it on top.",
"Val.Generic.81": "On the back of my neck, I have a tattoo of the alchemical symbol for Mercury. I learned about it during my metallurgical studies, though that's not why I got it.#$b#In classic astrology, Mercury is the one planet not designated male nor female. So, to me, the symbol is a means of expressing how I feel about my own presentation.",
"Val.Generic.82": "I never knew my mother or father growing up, I was raised by an adventurer named Wyatt. A good man with a hard life; he took me in and fostered my love for academia.#$b#He's retired in the Fern Islands, now. I call him twice a week, but he worries whenever I visit. Not sure how he'll react to my face...",
"Val.Generic.83": "The Adventurer's Guild wouldn't exist if all monsters were friendly. My body is a canvas of scars; I think that's proof enough there's a reason for concern.#$b#Shadow Folk are the only sapient creatures down there, and they have a fair enough reason to be violent.",
"Val.Generic.84": "I was delving with Wyatt at a pretty young age - too young, probably. But as a result, my skills are sharp and I plan to keep them that way.#$b#The number on my Adventurer's Guild badge is thirteen. I try not to think too hard about the nine I haven't met.",
"Val.Generic.85": "My favorite bands? Hm. Ghast is my number one. I have all of their albums in a few different prints each.#$b#But I really like who they've toured with, too. Dehaan, Molebeat, Colossus, Ash Mountain, Revenged Eightfold...",
"Val.Generic.86": "What kind of music are you into, @? I'm on the glam metal end of the spectrum, but my favorite band is more in the vein of ...'spooky pop-rock'.$9#$b#I have a lot of records stored under my bed, but I bet you a third of them are collector variants of the same few albums.$1",
"Val.Generic.87": "I need to clean the stylus on my record player. Haven't dusted the turntable in a bit, either. I'd best get on that!$1#$b#I keep the records I don't listen to often stored away. But sometimes, I get the urge to pull out a classic...$17",
"Val.Generic.88": "Have you ever read 'The Great Gatsbish? It's my favorite book of all time. It's relatively short and the prose is lovely, if you'd ever like to borrow my copy.$20#$b#It's about wanting to change the past. About obsession. About the masks we all wear, and how they're capable of cracking no matter how gilded they are.$25",
"Val.Generic.89": "I got this little bear figurine from a tchotchke shop across the street from a diner I went to... what was it called, Twede's? They had really good cherry pie.$22#$b#Anyway, I'm pretty sure it's haunted. It's got a certain look in it's eye. But I won't throw it away because I feel like that's somehow worse.$27",
"Val.Generic.90": "Emeritus keeps taking all my socks and burying them in the sand outside. I'm not sure why he does this; that is not a clever Pepper Rex by any means...", 
"Val.Generic.91": "Emeritus always looks like he just woke up from a nap. There's not a single thought behind those sleepy Pepper Rex eyes.",
"Val.Generic.92": "Emeritus keeps leaving his stable at night to sleep at the foot of the bed. He's about 300 pounds and thinks he weighs a quarter of that - not that I mind having a cuddly dinosaur around.", 
"Val.Generic.93": "Emeritus sometimes walks around crying with something in his mouth, usually a shirt or something. He'll give a thousand yard stare and I honestly just have no idea what to do in response.",
"Val.Generic.94": "Emeritus' favorite toys are these stuffed pumpkins that have squeakers inside. TI thought they were cute until he started playing with them exclusively at two in the morning.",
"Val.Generic.95": "Emeritus keeps breaking into the garbage as if he isn't fed two meals a day plus snacks. Pretty sure everything that goes down just melts from Pepper Rex fire.",
"Val.Generic.96": "I've never met an elf before Roslin - honestly, I thought they were entirely mythical. But they're just not native to the Ferngill Republic.#$b#Though, I've never seen a place called 'Álfheimr' on a map. Maybe she's just pulling my leg - who knows, I'm not willingly going to make her angry.",
"Val.Generic.97": "I visited Dandelion and Roslin because Coriander made them a care package and asked me to walk it up the mountain. I didn't mind the errand, but I walked in on Roslin arguing with Solomon.#$b#Dandelion ended it by picking her up and putting her on a bookshelf and greeting me like nothing was wrong.",
"Val.Generic.98": "How much time does Coriander put into maintaining her hair? How is it not fried by bleach? Where is she getting such saturated dyes?#$b#I'm just going to assume it's magic until I'm confronted with the truth. Even then, I may just turn away from it.",
"Val.Generic.99": "I had Coriander over the other day. She brought over a bunch of Ginger Beer, I made dinner, and we chatted video games - you should join us next time, @!",
"Val.Generic.100": "I saw Lorin smoking not one, but two, cigarettes. Everyone is entitled to their vices, but I'm pretty sure two-at-once is a diminishing return.",
"Val.Generic.101": "I took the long trek to visit Lorin the other day. We got wine drunk and pet the Owlcobos, so it was pretty much the best day ever.",
"Val.Generic.102": "Did you know Lorin falls asleep with crime shows on the television? Says it helps her sleep.#$b#Who in their right mind falls asleep to horror stories like that? Goodness, gracious.",
"Val.Generic.103": "Hector's really boisterous when [LocalizedText Strings/DN.SnS:HeShe]'s in a group, but when it's just him and I talking he gets a lot more solemn. Really thoughtful dude.#$b#I asked him about his dedication to Druidics, once. He just cryptically said he was 'born a tree with many rings'.",
"Val.Generic.104": "Odelia recently showed me some tinctures to help with minor wounds. She's a talented alchemist, and I appreciate her taking the time to share her techniques.#$b#She was kind enough to send me home with a bunch of supplies, so I plan to return the favor by bringing her some beach forage.",
"Val.Generic.105": "Hector says that Trolls are native to the mountains, entrusted by nature to protect them and the surrounding forests and wildlife.#$b#While I've always lived by the beach, I used to visit the Deep Mountains plenty as a kid. Always felt at home there, and now I know why. I don't plan to relocate; if anything, the 'charge' of my heritage is the Deep Dark.",
"Val.Generic.106": "Hey, @! I had some extra ore and hammered out some ingots. Figured I'd share.$1 #$action AddItem {{Random: (O)Copper_Bar, (O)Iron_Bar, (O)Gold_Bar, (O)Iridium_Bar}} {{Random: {{Range: 1,3}}}}",
"Val.Generic.107": "Hey, @! I collected an over-abundance of coal, and I figured I'd share the wealth. #$action AddItem (O)Coal {{Random: {{Range: 20,50}}}}",
"Val.Generic.108": "Hey, @! Got this when I cracked a geode, figured you might want it for the museum.$1 [538 539 540 541 542 543 544 545 546 547 548 549 550 551 552 553 554 555 556 557 558 559 560 561 562 563 564 565 566 567 568 569 570 571 572 573 574 575 576 577 578",
"Val.Generic.109": "Are you being safe in your dungeon delving, @? Here's something that'll help...$25 [349 351]",
"Val.Generic.110": "Hey, @! Guess what? I got you a treat, just in case you haven't gotten one for yourself today.$17#$action AddItem (O)DN.SnS_ChocolateOrange",
// SEASONAL
"Val.Spring.1": "It's getting warmer out. You can tell by the Spring in folks' step.$31",
"Val.Spring.2": "What did the florist say during springtime, @?... Business is blooming.$32",
"Val.Spring.3": "I've got a Spring in my step, @, how about you?$23 ",
"Val.Spring.4": "Now that the cold is gone, I'm feeling... like a tree. You know, very re-leafed.$17",
"Val.Spring.5": "How does the sun listen to music, @? Well... on the ray-dio, of course.$1",
"Val.Summer.1": "Howdy, @. Will I sea you on the beach this Summer?$31",
"Val.Summer.2": "Pardon my resting beach face, @. But now that you're here, anything is... popsicle.$32 [233]",
"Val.Summer.3": "Water you waiting for, @? Let's get everyone together and go swimming. The weather's just right!$23",
"Val.Summer.4": "I was reading a novel about a man trapped at sea, and you can say it made me very... em-ocean-al.$17",
"Val.Summer.5": "My favorite genre of book? Oh, it's fantasy, but in the Summer it's fanta-sea.$1",
"Val.Fall.1": "I could go for some mulled cider right now, or some roasted corn, or apple pie with some ice cream...$17",
"Val.Fall.2": "It's sunflower season, right? Do you cook the seeds? Oh, you could do that with pumpkins, too. It's delicious!$1",
"Val.Fall.3": "Are you an apple cider person, a pumpkin spice person, or a hot chocolate person? 'Tis the season for all the best warm drinks.$26",
"Val.Fall.4": "Don't blow a Jack o' Lantern out before midnight, @, Or you'll invite creatures of the night into your home. Good for you if you're doing it intentionally, though.$28",
"Val.Fall.5": "Life starts over again when it gets crisp in the Fall.$25",
"Val.Winter.1": "I have a really hard time in Winter. Spending time in the Deep Dark this time of year just makes it worse because of the lack of sunlight. It's... uh, snow joke.$24",
"Val.Winter.2": "Sorry if I give you the cold shoulder, @. I tend to be moody this time of year, and ...ice people out.$15",
"Val.Winter.3": "Guess you can say this dreary weather has me feeling really frost-rated. I really hate this yearly... Winter-uption.$11",
"Val.Winter.4": "Hey, @. Aren't you a sight for sore-ice? How are you holding up this season? Maintaining the farm this time of year must be easier sled than done.$27",
"Val.Winter.5": "Winter's challenging to get through, but I suppose everything has it's... highs and froze.$22",
// DATING DIALOGUE
"Val.Romance.1": "Howdy, Sunshine. I know you're very skilled, but please be careful in when you go dungeon delving. I'd be beside myself if anything happened to you, and if you want company, all you have to do is ask.$25#$b#Between Stygium and Radioactive Ore, there's so much to be wary of. Just stay vigilant, and keep your wits about you!$26 [349 351]",
"Val.Romance.2": "Date night idea: you and me, out in the desert, with nothing but a blanket, a bottle of wine, the stars- and that ginormous skeleton that's half buried in the sand and bleached white by the sun.$19",
"Val.Romance.3": "Hey, Sunshine. How about you come visit me by the cove? We'll practice your technique, your footwork...$17#$b#Do I think you need the guidance? No. Is this a thinly veiled excuse to work up a sweat with my favorite person? Absolutely.$19",
"Val.Romance.4": "Have you ever seen me throw knives, @? I'll prove I don't miss a mark. Maybe cold steel won't be the only thing pinned to a dartboard tonight.$19#$e#Actually, wait, I don't even have a dartboard. Is there one in the Inn? I don't think so. Maybe the Saloon?...$29",
"Val.Romance.5": "Why 'Sunshine'? Because it's always dark in the mines, and you're the first thing I want to see when I fight my way up. Love you, @.$16",
"Val.Romance.6": "You're just the person I wanted to see, Sunshine. I've had something I've been meaning to tell you.$32#$b#Actually, how about I show you instead, if you're not busy later? It's a message best delivered horizontal.$31",
"Val.Romance.7": "I tend not to go to the Saloon to drink; after all, brandy makes one randy, whiskey makes one frisky - by that logic, will wine make you mine?$19#$e#I mean, you're already mine, but... it sounded good for the bit.$27",
"Val.Romance.8": "You know, being a Troll has a few benefits. My tail is prehensile. I'm gifted with strength and dexterity. And! I come with my own handlebars.$19",
"Val.Romance.9": "You're my everything, Sunshine. When I look at you, I feel like I could take on the world.$17#$e#I don't mean to imply you make me feel violent, I just... I was just... trying to sound charming...$27",
"Val.Romance.10": "@, you have a rare smile with such a reassurance to it. You stop the world with your gaze, and you make those around you feel understood.$25",
"Val.Romance.11": "In a world full of the pursued, the pursuing, the busy and the tired, you rise above as a pillar of kindness. I love you, @.$25",
"Val.Romance.12": "Meeting you felt like a tuning fork struck a star. To have you to myself, now, feels nothing short of divine.$25",
"Val.Romance.13": "...I didn't have the easiest recovery after my mastectomy. The scars are still pretty sensitive, and the remaining breast tissue is often sore.$24#$b#They're aching right now, in fact. But you know what'd help? Your lips against them.$31#$e#Don't knock me for shooting my shot.$17",
"Val.Romance.14": "Ya'know, getting a mastectomy was a real load off my chest. The surgeon said I looked breast-taking, so I was really flat-tered.$17#$b#Not going to lie, I've had those jokes in the chamber for a while. Thanks for being a safe person for me to make them to, Sunshine.$9",
"Val.Romance.15": "If I'm being terribly honest, I've had my fair share of daydreams about you. Sometimes it's as mundane as making you coffee, or holding your hand on a walk.$17#$b#Other times it's more along the lines of 'I wonder how they'll look in my bed, between my sheets.'.$19#$e#I mean, I'd love to find out, if you're not busy.$31",
"Val.Romance.16": "Harvey said I spend so much time in the Deep Dark that I'm deficient in Vitamin D due to lack of sun exposure...$6#$b#You know what, I'm gonna give you three guesses as to where I was going to go with that joke.$28",
"Val.Romance.17": "You should come by for date night, Sunshine. I'll cook you nice dinner, whip up your drink of choice, and we'll curl up with Emeritus.$25#$b#Let me take care of you. With all that work you pour into %farm, you're more than deserving of a night of getting pampered.$4",
"Val.Romance.18": "How has the farm been coming along, Sunshine? If you need help with chores, I'm more than happy to oblige.$1#$b#All I ask is I get some time with %pet afterward.",
"Val.Romance.19": "How's %farm, Sunshine? You've come so far since moving here, it's so impressive. Dedication is one of your most attractive traits.$4",
"Val.Romance.20": "Give %pet a big ol' kiss on the head. You have to tell them it's from me, that part's very important.$0#$e#You can have a kiss too, Sunshine. You need only ask.$4",
"Val.Romance.21": "Hello, Sunshine. Here's a little something in case you go delving today. Please stay safe, alright? I love you.$25[349 351]",
"Val.Romance.22": "Let me know if you need your blade sharpened or your armor maintained, Sunshine. I know you can do it, but I'd love to take a task off your hands.$25",
"Val.Romance.23": "Are you made of copper and tellurium? Because you're Cu-Te. Maybe you're made of steel, because you've got my heart in a permanent melt.$26#$e#Oh, here's another. If you were a sword, you'd be Excalibur. Sharp, legendary, and cutting through my defenses.$28#$e#Last one. Are you a welder? Because our attraction is heating up.$19#$e#That's all I got for you, Sunshine. Don't worry, I'll be here all week.$17",
"Val.Romance.24": "You know what they say about Artificers, Sunshine. We get it hot, then hit it. We bang better, grind better. We know how to use our tools...$31#$b#Aren't you so glad you've let me forge a connection to your heart?$32",
"Val.Romance.25": "...You understand me, just as far as I've ever wanted to be understood. You believed in me, as you would like to believe in yourself.$25",
// MARRIAGE DIALOGUE
